2026-08-25T00:00:05Z (RFD66606-1079) 'AppSignal observability, and versitygw's removal
 # tags: rfd:details-title, rfd:no-final-newline
 Text:RFD1079  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:06Z (RFD66606-1079) '`Appsignal.Plug`, not raw OpenTelemetry, per the user's own direction. `use Appsignal.Plug` in `router.ex`, before `:match`, so it wraps every request. Config is entirely env-var driven (`APPSIGNAL_ACTIVE`, `APPSIGNAL_APP_NAME`, `APPSIGNAL_APP_ENV`, `APPSIGNAL_OTP_APP`), matching this project's existing pattern, no `config.exs` entry needed. `APPSIGNAL_PUSH_API_KEY` is a secret, in two places: the `APPSIGNAL_PUSH_API_KEY` GitHub Actions secret (the source of record), and a Fly secret the deploy workflow now `flyctl secrets set --stage`s from that GitHub secret on every run, not only the one time this session set it by hand.
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD1079  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:07Z (RFD66606-1079) '`versitygw` is removed outright, not deferred: no more build stage in `Dockerfile.fly`, no more process in `deploy/docker-entrypoint-fly.sh`, `VGW_ACCESS_KEY`/`VGW_SECRET_KEY` unset as Fly secrets.
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD1079  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:08Z (RFD66606-1079) 'RFD66606-1073 and RFD66606-1077 (both weftspun/request-for-discussion) decide Tigris over `versitygw`. RFD66606-1076 gives the `apps/` split that made `versitygw` unreachable from `usd_viewer_app` in the first place.
 # tags: rfd:related
 Text:RFD1079  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:09Z (RFD66606-1079) 'What removal costs
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD1079  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:10Z (RFD66606-1079) 'It cost nothing extra to run, colocated inside the already-billed machine, so removing it changes no bill, only dead code and a credential surface nothing reads anymore.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1079  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:11Z (RFD66606-1079) 'Why versitygw goes
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD1079  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:12Z (RFD66606-1079) 'Separately, RFD66606-1073's `versitygw` (RFD66606-1058's S3-API gateway) sat unused: RFD66606-1073 (weftspun/request-for-discussion) and RFD66606-1077 already decided Tigris replaces it, and RFD66606-1076 split `apps/usd_viewer_app/` onto its own Fly machine, which cannot reach `versitygw`'s loopback-only bind at all.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1079  1 LINE
 Text:Written
